Approved term	Definition	Avoid saying
Offer	Umbrella word for anything that lowers a price (a Promotion or a Discount).	"Deal", "coupon", "special"
Discount	An always-on price reduction on one product (amenity). No code. Example: $50 → $25 on weekdays.	"System discount" in customer-facing text
Promotion	A campaign-based offer with dates, limits and rules. Created on the Create Promotion screen. Comes as Promo Code or Automatic.	"Promo" alone when the type matters
Promo Code promotion	Customer must enter a code at checkout.	"Coupon code"
Automatic promotion	Applies by itself when the cart qualifies. No code.	"Auto discount", "no-code promo"
Promo code	The text the customer enters. Unique, letters/numbers only.	"Coupon", "voucher"
Display message	The text the customer sees describing the offer.	"Description", "title"
Applies to Full Cart	Toggle. ON = whole order is discounted. OFF = only the selected amenity.	"Cart level / product level" (use "Full cart" and "Amenity")
Amenity	The product or attraction the offer targets when Full Cart is OFF.	"Item", "SKU"
Priority	1 (highest) to 5 (lowest). Decides which offer is evaluated first and wins when offers compete.	"Rank", "weight"
Stackable	Whether the offer may combine with other offers.	"Combinable"
Stack group	A label that puts offers in competition. Within one group only one applies.	"Bucket", "category"
User type	Who qualifies: All Users, Members, Non-Members.	"Customer type"
Channel	Where the offer works: Web, POS or both.	"Platform", "source"
Draft	Saved, not live.	"Saved"
Published	Live. The rule is active in the engine.	"Active" (reserve "active" for the rule record)
Inactive	Turned off. The rule is deactivated.	"Deleted", "removed"
Rule (Drools rule)	The generated engine record that applies a published offer. Versioned.	"Script"
